The [4471 page](/kb/incidents/4471) says one issue, one fix. Reading the 427 merged reports
(as the desk counts them, from the export) against the tenant directory shows two more
problems merged in, neither with a ticket of its own. Neither is fixed by the queued parser
fix.

<Callout kind="warn">
Re-running the merge as one issue strands 39 reports — 34 reports of one bug, 5 of another —
with no ticket of their own.
</Callout>

## 1 · The v3 form's date hint (34 reports)

`booking-v3` prints **MM/DD/YYYY** under its date field, but every v3 tenant writes day
first: alder.physio (12 reports), copper.studio (11), pale.harbour (11, one twice in the
export). Their people type what the hint tells them, month first, and the form reads it the
tenant's way: day first. The date comes out flipped — the same symptom, a different cause.

16 of the 34 were tagged `parser` at intake; 18 `hint`; five more (R-41202, R-41209,
R-41236, R-41344, R-41620) the desk already reads one-day, in desk-notes.json. Seen
2026-04-17 → 2026-09-22, all in the `form` channel.

## 2 · One-day moves (5 reports)

Five reports merged into the parser ticket read as one-day moves, not month flips:

- R-41202 kettle.books — "Invite says Tuesday 12 May. Calendar says Monday 11 May."
- R-41209 alder.physio — "Every booking in June is one day off. Only June."
- R-41236 nine.lanterns — "The invite arrived before I made the booking."
- R-41344 pale.harbour — "Client in Lisbon got Tuesday. Client in Toronto got Monday."
- R-41620 lantern.row — "Tuesday 6 October showed as Monday."

The bodies point at more than one mechanism (a one-day move, a timezone, a queue race),
which is why they need their own ticket, not the parser fix. All five were tagged `parser`
at intake; the desk read them one-day in desk-notes.json but never filed them.

